                <pb facs="0076" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.1012 Anti-War/93 supp.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Owen</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-21T19:00:00-04:00">June 21, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Department’s 15, June 9, 1934, 3 p.m. The Argentine Anti-War Pact has just
                    been ratified by this Government, and you may express to the Danish Government
                    our sincere belief in the efficacy of the Pact and of our hope that the other
                    nations of the world will become signatories to it.</p>
                <p>Similar instructions are being sent to the Legations at Stockholm and Oslo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
